  "verdict_caveat": "`actor_uses_pixels` thresholds the MEDIAN of three corruptions at 30%. That threshold was calibrated on RGB_PROPRIO: none actors, whose ONLY input is the camera, so a corruption there removes everything. This run has RGB_PROPRIO='full', i.e. the actor also reads the privileged state, so it can ride the state through a corrupted frame and a genuinely pixel-using actor is EXPECTED to score well under 30%. The threshold under-reads in this regime and the median hides disagreement between the three corruptions. Read `performance_drop_fraction` condition by condition, together with the independent in-training `pixel_sensitivity` probe, rather than this boolean.",
